{"version":"activity-event.v1","id":"AEV-260906-4141f35070de20ac066c6f60","sequence":2,"timestamp":"2026-09-06T22:08:28.502659Z","actor":{"principal":{"availability":"unknown"},"agent":{"availability":"known","value":"claude"},"run":{"availability":"unknown"},"session":{"availability":"known","value":"42acde30-42a9-4e5e-a467-ec943234aebd"},"operator":{"availability":"unknown"}},"subject":{"element_id":"TASK-260907-2as5sx","element_type":"task"},"source":{"kind":"local_cli","entrypoint":"cmd.runMutate","request":{"availability":"unknown"}},"correlation_id":"COR-260906-bff4d7106513b9a63f2b1f31","causal_order":1,"operation":"content","changes":[{"field":"description","before":{"kind":"text","text":""},"after":{"kind":"text","text":"Close the section 8.4 absence-versus-failed-read collapse as a class rather than one site at a time. Five sites have now been found in three separate review cycles."}},{"field":"scope","before":{"kind":"text","text":"(define task scope)"},"after":{"kind":"text","text":"Section 8.4 makes absence and a failed read different facts, so a fallback defined for absence must not fire on a read failure. Sites found so far: readSkillsLedger (fixed in ee6743a2), readRootSurface (cycle-2 C2-B1), the KindPath snapshot read (cycle-4 C4-M1), and two more the cycle-6 reviewer observed without treating them as blocking: status.go:432 and status.go:521, alongside purgeHomes. The stage (c) producer answered honestly that nothing structural prevents a sixth: the sites read different manager-owned shapes through different helpers and no shared helper covers them. That answer was accepted for the leaf and is the reason for this task."}},{"field":"acceptance_criteria","before":{"kind":"text","text":"(define acceptance criteria)"},"after":{"kind":"text","text":"Either a shared read seam distinguishes absence from failure for every read of manager-owned state, or a test enumerates those read sites and asserts each distinguishes the two. The five known sites are covered either way, each proven by a narrowing mutant that collapses one of them and kills a named test. If a structural seam is judged infeasible, the report says why with the alternatives weighed rather than asserting vigilance."}}]}
